+
+What happens when something is missing (seen on Linux with Python 3.12.3, on ports other than 8765 and 8766; the author's notes are not in this repository): with the demo server not running, the desk prints `cannot reach the demo servers (are they running? see scripts/start_all)` (there is one demo server program; the message says "servers") and ends with exit code 1. With `PYTHONPATH=src` alone, the two `python -m` commands still work when started from the repository folder, because Python puts the current folder on the module path for `-m`; but `python scripts/crash_desk.py` does not have the current folder on its path, and with the demo server running it ends with exit code 1 and a RuntimeError that says the folder `demo_only` is missing (with the demo server not running it prints the "cannot reach" message instead). That is why `src:.` (the `:.` adds the repository folder, where `demo_only` is) is written in every command above except `feed.py`.
